                "url": "https://github.com/dletorey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 145 adds support for the Crash Reporting API; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Most of the BCD for this API has already been added; however, I wanted to add a data point for the <code class=\"notranslate\">crash</code> report type. The data for the different report types is contained under api.ReportingObserver.ReportingObserver.options_parameter.types_property, so I added it under there. This data is also used as the BCD for each report type dictionary; I'll need it when documenting <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/crash-reporting/#dictdef-crashreportbody\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">CrashReportBody</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a bit weird, as <code class=\"notranslate\">crash</code> reports aren't observed by reporting observers, but I think you can still specify them as a valid report type in the constructor <code class=\"notranslate\">types</code> list.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29475",
            "title": "Chrome 145 Crashing reporting, crash report type",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-20T11:18:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T08:26:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7944955?u=2561481b8ea6df6246494193d1a08e1d44386ac0&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome is shipping the Prompt API in 148. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I generated a schema from existing BCD and tested the JSON against the schema.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29473.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4257144079\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473\">#29473</a> and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4249385804\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43755\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43755/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43755\">mdn/content#43755</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29474",
            "title": "Chrome added Prompt API in 148 #29473",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-20T16:05:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T18:54:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jmedley",
                "url": "https://github.com/jmedley"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureUsage</code>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728</a>, and also see <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points for the <code class=\"notranslate\">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> in the places in which it appears.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29470",
            "title": "Chrome 146 WebGPU texture transient_attachment usage",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-20T11:30:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T15:44:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80624252?u=abb5f45720c0c7db48614fa1cfe4ed7032af0a36&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sets Safari's support for <code class=\"notranslate\">AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">partial</code>. The <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-public-key-easy\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web Authentication API specification</a> (since level 2 where it was first described in) states that user agents MUST support algorithm -7 (ES256), -8 (Ed25519), and -257 (RS256). However, WebKit only supports -7 (ES256) and returns <code class=\"notranslate\">null</code> for the other 2 algorithms.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/52dbebe20b922cab89928085f9dcfa8082a813e4/Source/WebCore/Modules/webauthn/AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.cpp#L162\">WebKit source code</a></li>\n<li>Tested on Safari 18.6 on macOS.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29458",
            "title": "Safari partially supports `AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()`",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-18T16:34:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-12T23:40:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pilcrowonpaper",
                "url": "https://github.com/pilcrowonpaper"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the linter, adding MDN urls for features that include the <code class=\"notranslate\">@@</code> prefix.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ensures that <code class=\"notranslate\">@@iterator</code> etc gets an <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code> automatically.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Triggered via <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4233820489\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29441\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441\">#29441</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29454",
            "title": "fix(lint): add MDN urls for features with `@@` prefix",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T14:55:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-10T21:23:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AFAICT, <code class=\"notranslate\">fetch()</code> has always supported a request <code class=\"notranslate\">body</code>, but only recently acquired <code class=\"notranslate\">ReadableStream</code> bodies. This PR reorganizes the data to make this more obvious.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR doesn't actually create any new data; it copies or moves it.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.fetch.init_body_parameter</code> copies the support data from <code class=\"notranslate\">api.fetch</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Request.Request.init_body_parameter</code> copies the support data from <code class=\"notranslate\">api.Request.Request</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.fetch.body_readablestream</code> moved to <code class=\"notranslate\">api.fetch.init_body_parameter.readablestream</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Request.request_body_readablestream</code> moved to <code class=\"notranslate\">api.Request.Request.init_body_parameter.readablestream</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Where required, I changed descriptions and added spec URLs.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3425893891\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3361\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/3361/hovercard?comment_id=4216947419&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/3361#issuecomment-4216947419\">web-platform-dx/web-features#3361 (comment)</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29451",
            "title": "Clean up Fetch `body` data",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-21T11:09:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-10T18:04:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removes the CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family</code> subfeatures for generic fonts, because no browser actually supports them.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The collector tests at <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/tests/css/properties/font-family\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/tests/css/properties/font-family</a> fail in Chrome 146, Firefox 149, and Safari 26.4.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29246.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4067860451\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246/hovercard?comment_id=4067872654&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246#issuecomment-4067872654\">#29246 (comment)</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29439",
            "title": "Remove generic font-family features",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-09T12:50:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-09T12:50:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">update-browser-releases</code> script for Safari, adding a <code class=\"notranslate\">\"preview\"</code> entry for Safari TP corresponding to the latest release in the <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/category/safari-technology-preview/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Safari TP blog</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Rather than guessing the next Safari release version, uses the version \"preview\", which is also used in the data.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29421",
            "title": "feat(update-browser-releases): track Safari TP release",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-07T15:18:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-07T14:42:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removes a Firefox note from CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;gradient&gt;</code> which is out of context, and no longer relevant.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/18503#issuecomment-4171174737\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/18503/hovercard\">this comment</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #18503.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1514896026\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/18503\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/18503/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/18503\">#18503</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29388",
            "title": "Remove obsolete Firefox note from CSS `<gradient>`",
